<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>If you own a manufactured home in Citra, there's a good chance it sits on an acreage lot where nobody has looked under it in years. That's normal out here. North Marion County is horse country, homes are spread out, and a single-wide that went up in the 80s or 90s has often been riding on the same block piers ever since. Sandy soil shifts, wood shims compress, and one day the doors start sticking and the floor develops a slope you can feel in your socks.</p><p>Ocala Level Pros relevels manufactured homes across Citra, Sparr, Anthony, Fort McCoy, and the Orange Lake area. We check the whole frame with a water level, reset or replace piers that have sunk or cracked, and leave you with a written record of the work. Most jobs are done in a day. Call <strong>(352) 247-3105</strong> for a free written estimate, or read up on <a href="/mobile-home-leveling-cost/">what leveling typically costs</a> before we come out.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Do in Citra</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">Services for Citra Properties</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E4DCC8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(22,51,44,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Poppins',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#16332C;margin:0 0 8px;">Mobile Home Releveling</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">We shoot the frame at every pier, then shim and reblock until the home reads level end to end. Common fix for Citra homes on sandy acreage that have settled unevenly over decades.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E4DCC8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(22,51,44,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Poppins',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#16332C;margin:0 0 8px;">Pier and Blocking Repair</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Cracked caps, leaning block stacks, and piers that have sunk into soft ground get rebuilt on solid footing. We see a lot of this under older single-wides off US 301 that haven't been touched since setup.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E4DCC8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(22,51,44,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Poppins',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#16332C;margin:0 0 8px;">Tie-Down and Anchor Replacement</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Rural homes that sat untouched for 20 or 30 years often have rusted straps and loose anchors in sandy soil. We inspect, retension, and replace them to current standards. More detail on our <a href="/mobile-home-tie-downs-ocala/">tie-down page</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E4DCC8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(22,51,44,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Poppins',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#16332C;margin:0 0 8px;">Skirting and Vapor Barrier Work</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Long-neglected skirting lets moisture and animals under a Citra home, which speeds up the settling we get called for. After leveling, we can repair <a href="/mobile-home-skirting-ocala/">skirting</a> and replace a torn <a href="/vapor-barrier-ocala/">vapor barrier</a> in the same trip.</p>
      </div>
</div>
